38. In Monroe's Motivated Sequence. the "satisfaction" step is designed toA. highlight the urgency of the issueB. explain the solution to the problemCl. introduce the main topic of the speechD" help the audience understand the outcome
What error in reasoning is exemplified in the following statement?"If we let students skip homework just once, soon they will stop studying entirely, fail alltheir exams, and never get a good job. Society will collapse because no one will beeducated!"A. False causeB. Slippery slopeC. Invalid analogyD" HastygeneralizationWhat error in reasoning is exemplified in the following statement?"We should continue teaching students with chalkboards instead of tablets because schoolshave been doing it this way for hundreds of years. If it worked before, it must be the bestway to teach now."A. False causeB. Ad HominemC. invalid analogyD. Appeal to tradition
39.
40"
